      "obligation": "refuter:126:1",
      "id": "lem-tgrx-locally-finite-relative-chain-model",
      "location": "Step 3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 3.1 says the local class “has the nonzero local class by its supplied compact relative fundamental-class property and [F4].” The cited definition supplies the local generator for the compact manifold N_p, hence in H_n(N_p,N_p\\{p\\}; Z_2), while the lemma needs the class in H_n(Y,Y\\{p\\}; Z_2). The proof does not state the inclusion/excision isomorphism between these groups. Since N_p contains a neighborhood of p, excision supplies this short step.",
